<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean 1996 electronics exports seen falling.</title>
<headline>S.Korean 1996 electronics exports seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's electronics exports are expected to fall 4.4 percent year-on-year in 1996, the first drop in 14 years, the Electronics Industries Association of Korea said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A report from the association said customs-cleared exports of electronics products were expected to total $41.67 billion for the year, down from $43.59 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Officials at the association said sharp falls in the international prices of memory chips would be the biggest factor behind the sluggish exports.</p>
</text>
